**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A promoted library entry says where it was fitted (001 §I 'Promote to library mints the material's next version in the database, with provenance "fitted in kit K, study S, run R"'; 001 §L 'Publishing: … material or black-box object → Promote to library'; the S11.5 brief 'add an EntryProvenance case here if none fits'). None fits: `UserProvenance` carries nothing and `KitImportProvenance` names the kit alone (`LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, steps 24, 91). The study and the fit run are named by the file stems the kit stores them under (001 §A), because `StudyName` and `FitRunName` are declared after this file (steps 214, 358) and their `fileStem` members (steps 358, 383) are how a kit names them; nothing is moved. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `EntryProvenance` (steps 24, 91) gains a sixth case, `FitProvenance of EntryFitInfo`, declared together with `and EntryFitInfo = { kit : KitId; studyStem : FileStem; fitRunStem : FileStem }`: the kit the fit ran in (step 24's `KitId`) and the stems of the study's `<study>.study-json` and of the fit run's `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json`, the files that reproduce the fitted values (001 §I 'Old results stay reproducible because each fit run stores its parameter vector'). A fitted entry belongs to the user: `protection` answers `UserManaged`, `categoryOrigin` answers `UserCategory`, and `attributionOpt` (step 113) answers `None`, because a fit carries no licence. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs` (steps 63, 91): `kindValue` answers 6 for a fit and `catalogueIdOpt` answers `None`, because a fitted entry ships in no catalogue. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json` (steps 30, 91): the provenance definition gains a sixth shape, exactly what the serializer writes for `FitProvenance`: `kit` a GUID, and `studyStem` and `fitRunStem` non-empty strings. The entry schemas keep version 1, because no entry file has been released (.spec-md §7). Any other complete match on `EntryProvenance` that FS0025 reports answers a fit as it answers `UserProvenance`. No other case, member, converter or schema changes; the promotion builds the case (step 407). (4) Tests. `LibraryEntryFilesTests`' `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` also covers a `FitProvenance` of a test-local `KitId` with `FileStem "QZ-LR"` and `FileStem "QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z"`: it is `UserManaged` and `UserCategory`; its `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none` (step 113) also answers `None` for it. `EntryFileJsonTests`' `every provenance round-trips through an entry file` gains a material under that `FitProvenance`; it round-trips through its entry file, and its decoder answers the material.

**Acceptance.** After the provenance lands, `EntryProvenance` MUST hold `FitProvenance of EntryFitInfo` (the kit, the study's file stem and the fit run's file stem), user-managed with no attribution, stored with provenance kind 6 and no catalogue, and written and read back in an entry file under `library-common.schema.json`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the widened `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed`, `a pulled entry and its forks carry its licence's attribution, and every other provenance none` and `every provenance round-trips through an entry file`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
